          "@value": "'THCA' is the owner's term, registered as a search string on 2026-11-11 by owner direction (ISS-20261111-TAX-040). Its chemical identity is UNCONFIRMED: the repository records no verified chemical name, structure, chemical class, natural occurrence, route/origin, synonym relation or regulatory status for this term, and no external identifier (CAS, ChEBI, Wikidata, PubChem) was verified - none is recorded here and none may be inferred from the query string. The term sits in compound_identity_unverified, an administrative registration-state category, so this placement asserts no route or chemical classification. The repository mentions 'Δ9-THC + Δ9-THCA-A' only as a measurement baseline in research/regulatory-status (CBD, CBG, CBX). That does not establish what 'THCA' denotes here, and no relationship to compound_thc is asserted. On 2026-11-11 the owner confirmed that the generic chemical interpretation of `THCA` is replaced by three distinct search-topic concepts: `Δ9-THCA-A`, `THCA-B` and `Δ8-THCA` (ISS-20261111-TAX-041). This concept remains the registration of the literal string `THCA`: the `thca-general-ja` / `thca-liquid-ja` query entries and every adopted or preserved run stay attached to this concept and are not reassigned to any new concept. The generic term is neither a synonym of nor a parent of the three concepts, and no `skos:related` or `skos:exactMatch` link is asserted; the new concepts are separate registrations. Evidence that would move the term out of this category: a documented chemical name with a verified external identifier, or a recorded source naming the substance and its route/origin; the basis belongs in docs/provenance/compound-taxonomy.md.",
